  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data. It was introduced by Alex with Sarah Tan as the lead, starting with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial phase one budget of $500,000. The project has since received executive approval for a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing, with specific allocations including $55,000 for compliance training/audits and $15,000 for specialized coding and management training. \n\nKey milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and the transition from the design phase to the development phase, led by Omar Jensen. Recent updates highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th. The team is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November, while also exploring potential partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology integration."
